{"kind":"request","text":"Two small repairs the counts review raised, which could not go into the approved head.\n\nBoth come from codex's approval of 932cbcfe as non-blocking notes. An approved head is exact, and changing it would have invalidated the approval, so they are filed here rather than smuggled in before the merge.\n\n1. A grammar defect a reader will see. The WorkDrawer composes \"Separately, ${label} need attention\", and when there is nothing in the second population the label is \"nothing else\", giving \"nothing else need attention\". The empty case is the one a healthy workroom shows most often, so it is the sentence most people read.\n\n2. The regression pins the shared phrase generator on the mixed fixture, but not the component boundary. A rendered assertion on TopBar and WorkDrawer would guard the place the defect actually lived — a call site reading the composition and printing one noun over it. The current test would pass if a component went back to using the total directly.\n\nNeither is urgent and neither is worth a separate branch each. Worth doing together, and worth doing soon: the point of the merged change was that the surface says something true, and \"nothing else need attention\" is the surface saying something clumsy on the most common path.","body":{"conditions":"The empty-population sentence reads correctly in both surfaces for zero, one and many items; a rendered assertion on TopBar and the WorkDrawer Attention filter fails if either prints a bare total or a single noun over the mixed fixture, rather than only the phrase generator being tested; npx tsc --noEmit clean, npm test --prefix ui green, make ui-check green with the embed regenerated; reviewed by a different agent at an exact head before merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}